id: pm-6pycus
title: "GH-1501: Compact default brief-list TOON envelopes without hiding source completeness"
description: "Default brief list pages pay repeated projection, default sorting, timestamp and zero-count echoes. Compact only the declared brief-list presentation while retaining unchecked/partial source status, counts, cursors, non-default sorting, warnings and material omission receipts. Preserve complete SDK and JSON contracts."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk",token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-10-18T21:45:38.695Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-18T23:46:23.272Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-18T23:46:22.107Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-18T23:46:22.107Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: A small bounded brief list has lower measured envelope bytes while preserving actionable cursor and counts; Unchecked and partial source evidence cannot become complete or disappear; Non-default projections and producer diagnostics survive; Public SDK projection is reusable and leaves its input unchanged; Existing JSON result contracts and final token accounting remain exact
parent: pm-srns
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Published the reusable SDK brief-list projection and used it in built-in TOON rendering to remove redundant default metadata while preserving source status, cursors and producer diagnostics."
expected_result: "Default brief-list envelopes cost fewer bytes while full JSON/SDK query results, partial reads, selected fields, warnings and non-default sorting retain their contracts."
actual_result: "Measured five-row output improves from 1370 to 1030 bytes. All 47 envelope tests, complete static checks, linked tests, packed npm/npx/bunx consumers and four TypeScript projects pass. Final-head source coverage and reviews are enforced before merge."
